Round complete. Both deliverables are in: `impl/d1_twiddle.c` (full AVX-512 rewrite + adoption block v2) and a new "Round d1_r2" section appended to `strategies/d1_twiddle.md`. All 14 graded chained gates pass (worst margin 15×), single-call correctness is 1–3.4e-16 everywhere, output is bitwise repeatable, and every one of my 28 cells is 1.9–4.5× faster than r1 in a same-core A/B. What I borrowed is attributed: d1_pow2's cmul idiom, first-stage schedule, per-transform chain blocking, and Newton-map recipe (now safe because my twiddles are exact); d1_batchlane's ymm-autovectorization diagnosis. The adoption block now generates d1_pow2's twiddle format for any radix (`d1tw_stage_bc`/`d1tw_stage_s1bc`), so the exact generator is a drop-in for them next round.

**Summary line:** AVX-512 mixed-radix Stockham with exact broadcast-pair twiddle tables, across-p first stage, per-transform fused-map chain (rsqrt14+Newton+residual map) — wallaby best at L=32: 0.018 µs B=1 / 0.019 µs B=512 (chained 0.063), and at L=16384: 31.2 µs B=1 / 35.8 µs B=64 (chained 46.7/47.9); rel L2 ≤ 3.4e-16, chain gates all PASS ≥15× margin.
